It could happen, but the odds are quite slim.  Parts of the odds depend
on your AC (and so I lack the patience to calculate them), but the parts
that are fixed (assuming, for the sake of argument, a charisma of 18) are:
* AD_SSEX attack removing your cloak: 1 in 10.
* Bullwhip disarm attempt working: 3 in 20 (zero if your weapon is
  cursed).
* Rodney's amulet-theft attack working: 1 in 20; if you do not have the
  real Amulet, then he will go for your quest artifact.
* Rodney selecting Touch of Death: 3 in (current number of hit dice);
  starts at about 1 in 10 and decreases with the number of times you've
  killed Rodney.
* Rodney's Touch of Death killing you: (Rodney's HD - 13) in (Rodney's
  HD); starts at 17 in 30 and increases with the number of times you've
  killed Rodney.

So... with the necessary monsters next to you and due to act, an 18
charisma, an uncursed weapon, a level 30 Rodney, and the Amulet of
Yendor not in your inventory, we're starting at odds of 51 in 120000
(about 1 in 2353), before taking any account of whether the attacks
that require a to-hit roll actually hit you. (*That* calculation is a
complete headache because of the random AC factor.)

If you're wearing a ring of adornment sufficient to get you to Cha 20,
or Magicbane is cursed, you cannot be thus deprived of MR.

Also, I have an unsubstantiated feeling that monsters summoned by other
monsters don't get to act in the gametick in which they are summoned.
